title: Hermes Atlas Evolution
layout: balanced
---

# Atlas Evolution 0.13.0
> A Hermes plugin that learns from repeat tool failures. 28,226 lines of Python, MIT licence. Colours: green = carries over to Nimbalyst, yellow = carries over with a gap, red = Hermes only.

## 1 Signals {color: yellow}
> Collects what goes wrong. Nimbalyst stores every tool call in ai_agent_messages, but nothing reads failures out of it yet.
- Hooks it listens to {tags: hermes}
  - post_tool_call: failed tool calls
  - pre_llm_call and post_llm_call: turn timing
  - post_api_request and api_request_error
  - on_session_end, on_session_finalize
  - on_skill_lifecycle: skill use
  - subagent_start, post_compaction
- What it records
  - Tool name
  - One of 22 failure classes
  - Short detail
  - Owner corrections
- 14-day history replay seeds the first pass
- Modules: signals, logwatch, backfill, telemetry, operations
- Nimbalyst fit {color: yellow, status: todo}
  > get_session_coaching_signals keeps tool names and counts only, with no error field (sessionCoachingSignals.ts:33). A failure reader is a core change.

## 2 Lessons {color: green}
> The core idea. A repeat failure becomes a short "when X, do Y" rule.
- Rule: 3+ hits on 2+ days or sessions
- Fixed templates per failure class
- Reflector: a model drafts lessons with no template
  - Drafts always wait for the owner
- Modes
  - auto: goes live after 2 hits in the owner's own turns
  - otherwise: waits as a candidate
- Lesson record (experience.py:63)
  - signature, tool, klass, hint, origin, status, text
  - shown, hints, verdict, rate_before, rate_after
  - baseline_failures, baseline_calls
- Modules: lessons, reflector, hints, packs
- Nimbalyst fit {color: green, status: idea}
  > New evolution extension. Lesson text as nimbalyst-memory facts.

## 3 Delivery {color: yellow}
> How the agent sees active lessons.
- Prompt section, 1,400 characters at most
- Hint added to a failing tool result (tool_hints on)
- Optional agent tool: hermes_atlas_evolution_lessons
- Nimbalyst fit {color: yellow, status: question}
  > registerContextProvider only logs (ExtensionLoader.ts:1026). Workaround: a marked section in a memory file Claude Code reads.

## 4 Measurement {color: green}
> Checks whether each change helped.
- Lesson verdict: 14 days before vs 14 days after
  - effective, ineffective, inconclusive
  - auto mode retires an ineffective lesson
- Change experiments: 7 days before vs after
  - config edits, skill edits
- Not yet tested over weeks of real use
- Modules: experiments, evolve, insights, evolution_index
- Nimbalyst fit {color: green, status: idea}
  > The part memory-spike learn and nimbalyst-coach both lack.

## 5 Proposals {color: green}
> Anything bigger than a lesson waits for the owner.
- Each has risk, evidence, exact command
- Only the owner approves, in a terminal
  - Refuses when an agent marker is set
- Plugin runs only lessons, skill_lock, some environment fixes
- Every action logged with an undo
- skill_rollback opens when a skill change regressed
- Modules: proposals, decisions, explain
- Nimbalyst fit {color: green, status: idea}
  > Tracker items. The owner moves the status.

## 6 Schedule and cost {color: green}
- Autopilot pass about hourly
- Weekly digest cron job
- Self-cost meter per hook
- Modules: autopilot, selfcost, billing, report
- Nimbalyst fit {color: green, status: idea}
  > automations extension for the schedule. BackendSessionsService.getUsage for cost.

## 7 Storage {color: blue}
- evolution.sqlite3, schema 8
- settings.json
- 90-day retention
- Tables: lesson, change, proposal

## 8 Hermes upkeep {color: red}
> Hermes-only. Skip for Nimbalyst.
- guard: blocks commands that kill Hermes
- doctor, hermes_care, environment
- gateway repair, fleet_update, system_update
- memory_care: MEMORY.md and USER.md dedupe
- skill_health, radar
- ecosystem: Hermes plugin catalog
- Dashboard tab, menu, admin, cli, i18n

## Already on this machine {color: purple}
- memory-spike learn
  > Writes "failed command, then working command" lessons. No measurement, no retirement.
- nimbalyst-coach
  > Reads session signals and recommends changes. No failure classes, no verdicts.
